          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What code would that be recorded under?",
          "answer": "If a diagnosis of diabetes has been made, it would be recorded under codes such as E11 for Type 2 diabetes. Diabetes mellitus in general falls within the E08-E13 range in Chapter 4 of the ICD-10-CM, which covers endocrine, nutritional, and metabolic diseases (ICD-10-CM Chapter 4: endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases (E00-E89)).\n\nHowever, if a full diagnosis of diabetes has not been established, elevated glucose levels, including prediabetes, would be found in the blood-findings block of Chapter 18 of the ICD-10-CM (Symptoms, signs and abnormal findings), within the R70-R79 range. Prediabetes and abnormal glucose findings that do not meet the criteria for a diabetes diagnosis are not coded as E11 (Coding type 2 diabetes: E11 and its complication subcategories).\n\nA clinician would be able to provide the exact code based on your diagnosis.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n[sources: coding-type-2-diabetes-e11, coding-icd10-chapter-04-endocrine, coding-icd10-chapter-18-symptoms]",
